{
  "version": "3",
  "_README": [
    "Declared synthetic graph for offline retrieval evaluation (eval/graph_world.py).",
    "",
    "Ground truth is KNOWN because the world is declared, so a case can assert what traversal must",
    "reach without any human labelling. That gates retrieval BEHAVIOUR in CI \u2014 distinct from",
    "retrieval RELEVANCE on real users, which still needs labels (retrieval_cases.json).",
    "",
    "EVERY relationship type below is a REAL type from the generated ontology manifest, with its real",
    "traversability. v1 of this file invented plausible-sounding types (CONFLICTS_WITH, SUPPORTS,",
    "EVIDENCES) and _validate_rel_types would have rejected all of them \u2014 a fixture that cannot be",
    "traversed proves nothing. Verified against the manifest; a drift gate keeps that honest.",
    "",
    "Two tenants on purpose. user-b's nodes are given titles that score HIGHLY on user-a's queries,",
    "so a leak would be found by the vector seeding rather than merely being possible in theory.",
    "",
    "a-goal-retire -RELATED_TO- a-unrelated-pet is deliberately NON-traversable (RELATED_TO is",
    "traversable=false in the manifest). A case asserts the pet never appears: the dragnet guard.",
    "",
    "v3: finance nodes use domain 'financial', the CANONICAL value \u2014 normalize_domain('finance')",
    "returns 'financial', so storing 'finance' makes a node unreachable through the domain filter",
    "while retrieval reports success. That is the data-side form of the defect the engine comment",
    "calls out as having made 71% of the corpus unreachable. v2 of this fixture reproduced it exactly."
  ],
